    "note": "Introduced version. Sec. 2 adds a long 'assault weapon' definition to RCW 9.41.010 (named models plus feature tests); not quoted. Sec. 3(2) lists exemptions (military/law enforcement sales, out-of-state sales through dealers, inheritance). Possession is not banned."
  },
  "operative_text": "NEW SECTION Sec. 3 (new RCW section in chapter 9.41): (1) No person in this state may manufacture, import, distribute, sell, or offer for sale any assault weapon, except as authorized in this section.\nNEW SECTION Sec. 3 (new RCW section in chapter 9.41): (3) A person who violates this section is guilty of a gross misdemeanor.\nNEW SECTION Sec. 4 (new RCW section in chapter 9.41): (2) A violation of section 3 of this act is an unfair or deceptive act or practice or unfair method of competition in the conduct of trade or commerce for purposes of the consumer protection act, chapter  19.86 RCW."
